/**
 * profileSheet.ts: the words of the Light and Dark profile set in each export
 * language.
 *
 * One row per phrase: English, Spanish (Mexico), Portuguese (Brazil), French,
 * German. English is the source, and a row with a language missing fails the
 * build. The sentences other modules write (the legend, the provenance, the
 * height reference) are matched to their English row as the sheet is drawn, so
 * there is one English wording; a test draws every state of the sheet in every
 * language and fails on a sentence with no row.
 *
 * Parameters: `{n}` is a figure, rewritten in the number style; `{t_x}` is a
 * phrase with a row of its own; `{l_x}` is a list holding such phrases;
 * `{u_x}` is copied exactly (a name, a code, a time, text the user typed).
 *
 * Drafts until a geomatics reviewer signs them off (`reviewed` in
 * languages.ts); until then every sheet says so in its footer.
 */
